   344	def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
   345	    """
   346	    Use an edge palette to keep/fill matched hollow sprites, delete unmatched ones, then crop away the palette strip.
   347	
   348	    Input structure:
   349	    - The full grid has a dominant background border and one isolated 2xN or Nx2 palette sitting on a single edge.
   350	    - Away from that edge are hollow single-color sprites; some border colors appear on the palette key side and one
   351	      hollow distractor border color does not.
   352	
   353	    Rule:
   354	    - Detect the edge palette and read it as a border-color to fill-color mapping.
   355	    - For each enclosed background hole outside the palette, look at its surrounding border color on the original grid.
   356	      If that border color is a palette key, fill the hole with the mapped color; otherwise erase the touching sprite
   357	      component back to background.
   358	    - After all fills and deletions are resolved on the full grid, crop off the entire 2-cell strip that carried the
   359	      palette.
   360	
